# Checking a password the user typed into AppLocker's own dialog.
#
# Deliberately NOT "@include common-auth": on Ubuntu that stack begins with
# pam_fprintd (timeout=15), so the dialog would wait at the reader for 15s
# before it even looked at what was typed — and a finger touch would satisfy a
# call whose whole question is "is this the typed password correct?".
#
# shortcut: pam_unix only, so a password kept outside /etc/shadow (LDAP, sssd,
# AD) won't verify here; delete this file and the daemon falls back to the full
# `sudo` stack, fprintd wait included.
auth     required   pam_unix.so
account  required   pam_unix.so
